INSERT INTO `news` VALUES (1, 'Sales of the NFC wristband, which provides health information, have far exceeded expectations', '<p style=\"text-align: justify; font-family: \'Arial\', sans-serif; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 16px; color: #333;\">\r\n  In today\'s era of rapid digital development, scientific and technological products are constantly penetrating into all aspects of our lives, bringing convenience and security to our lives. Recently, a Florida tech startup called Sharewear launched an innovative bracelet product based on NFC (Near Field Communication) technology, aiming to provide vulnerable people with more convenient and secure access to health information management and emergency contact information.\r\n</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify; font-family: \'Arial\', sans-serif; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 16px; color: #333;\">\r\n  Amanda Anderson, founder and CEO of Sharewear, said the product was inspired by her concern for protecting family members\' health information. Anderson\'s father-in-law had multiple illnesses, and the family was concerned that medical personnel wouldn\'t be able to quickly access all of his health information in an emergency. This problem prompted Anderson to start thinking about how to use technology to solve the plight of such vulnerable people in health information management.\r\n</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify; font-family: \'Arial\', sans-serif; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 16px; color: #333;\">\r\n  After in-depth research, Anderson found that existing medical emergency bracelets can print or etch some basic information, but for people with a lot of health information, it often can\'t all be displayed on the bracelet. In addition, there is a risk that the printed code will be rubbed or peeled. Therefore, she decided to use NFC technology to create a new bracelet product.\r\n</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify; font-family: \'Arial\', sans-serif; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 16px; color: #333;\">\r\n  Sharewear\'s NFC bracelet has a 13.56MHz NFC chip inside, which is encoded with a unique ID. Users can connect the band to their digital profile via their smartphone and Sharewear software. The profile contains health details that the user would like to be known for in an emergency, allergy information, special needs, and phone numbers for emergency contacts. Once a bystander finds that the person wearing the bracelet is in need, they simply click the NFC symbol on the bracelet with their mobile phone and can automatically jump to the URL page to view the relevant information.\r\n</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify; font-family: \'Arial\', sans-serif; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 16px; color: #333;\">\r\n  In addition to basic health information management features, Sharewear\'s NFC bracelet also offers an optional subscription service. By spending $4.99 a month, users can get more services. For example, when someone taps a finger ring with a smartphone, the software collects data and sends an alert to parents or other relatives via text message about the event, as well as the geographic location of the device that reads the bracelet. This feature is especially useful for parents, who can keep track of their children\'s safety.\r\n</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify; font-family: \'Arial\', sans-serif; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 16px; color: #333;\">\r\n  It is worth mentioning that Sharewear\'s NFC bracelet is not only suitable for vulnerable people, but also can be used as a social and business networking tool. Users can set their health information as password protected according to their needs, so as to avoid being obtained by others at inappropriate times such as business occasions. At the same time, they can also turn off the function when needed for activities such as commercial marketing.\r\n</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify; font-family: \'Arial\', sans-serif; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 16px; color: #333;\">\r\n  Since its launch, Sharewear\'s NFC bracelet has received a lot of attention and praise. Seven law enforcement agencies and fire districts in Volusia and Flagler counties have begun purchasing the wristbands for public use. In addition, Sharewear has contracted with the Volusia County School District and the County Sheriff\'s Office to provide 500 bracelets for school-age children with special needs. Anderson said that the sales of this wristband far exceeded the company\'s expectations, and in the future they will continue to promote and educate the public, so that more people understand and accept NFC technology.\r\n</p>\r\n', 2, '/api/personal-heath/v1.0/file/getFile?fileName=news pic/1.jpg', NULL, 0, '2024-09-01 15:40:04', 1);
INSERT INTO `news` VALUES (2, 'Disease, like a cunning hunter lurking in the dark, is always ready to attack us', '<p style=\"text-align: justify; font-family: \'Arial\', sans-serif; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 16px; color: #333;\">In the past, as China\'s economy rapidly developed, many people\'s living standards and material conditions improved significantly. However, behind this rapid development, some neglected issues have been hidden, with health problems being one of the most prominent. As the economic growth slows and society gradually becomes more harmonious, people are beginning to realize that health is an even more important part of life.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify; font-family: \'Arial\', sans-serif; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 16px; color: #333;\"><strong>The health data of Chinese people is shocking!</strong></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify; font-family: \'Arial\', sans-serif; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 16px; color: #333;\">Through careful collection and organization, we have obtained a set of detailed data about the health status of Chinese people. These numbers are not just cold statistics, but like the voices of vibrant lives telling us about the preciousness of health.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify; font-family: \'Arial\', sans-serif; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 16px; color: #333;\">Hypertension — 160-170 million people</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify; font-family: \'Arial\', sans-serif; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 16px; color: #333;\">Hyperlipidemia — over 100 million people</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify; font-family: \'Arial\', sans-serif; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 16px; color: #333;\">Diabetic patients — 92.4 million people</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify; font-family: \'Arial\', sans-serif; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 16px; color: #333;\">Overweight or obesity — 70 million to 200 million people</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify; font-family: \'Arial\', sans-serif; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 16px; color: #333;\">Abnormal blood lipids — 160 million people</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify; font-family: \'Arial\', sans-serif; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 16px; color: #333;\">Fatty liver patients — 120 million people</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify; font-family: \'Arial\', sans-serif; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 16px; color: #333;\">Every 30 seconds, one person is diagnosed with cancer.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify; font-family: \'Arial\', sans-serif; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 16px; color: #333;\">Every 30 seconds, one person is diagnosed with diabetes.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify; font-family: \'Arial\', sans-serif; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 16px; color: #333;\">Every 30 seconds, at least one person dies from cardiovascular and cerebrovascular diseases.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify; font-family: \'Arial\', sans-serif; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 16px; color: #333;\">Behind these cold numbers are the pain and helplessness of countless families. They silently tell a cruel truth: in the busy life, we often neglect our health in the pursuit of money and material comforts. When health problems silently build up, we only realize the danger too late!</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify; font-family: \'Arial\', sans-serif; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 16px; color: #333;\"><strong>Establishing a good health concept</strong></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify; font-family: \'Arial\', sans-serif; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 16px; color: #333;\">The fast-paced modern life is like an invisible hand, pushing us forward, yet inadvertently causing major changes in our lifestyles and eating habits. Irregular sleep patterns, high-fat and high-salt diets, etc., are quietly eroding our health, casting the shadow of chronic diseases over our lives.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify; font-family: \'Arial\', sans-serif; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 16px; color: #333;\">More critically, our level of attention to health is still far from sufficient. In the past, people focused intently on economic development and improving material conditions, forgetting that health is the foundation of life. What we need is not just the advancement of medical technology, but the deep-rooted health concepts and conscious health behaviors.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify; font-family: \'Arial\', sans-serif; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 16px; color: #333;\">Health is urgent for everyone. We must cherish our bodies and constantly remind ourselves that health is the most important. Don’t wait until we lose our health before regretting it.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify; font-family: \'Arial\', sans-serif; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 16px; color: #333;\"><strong>Supplying Peptides is Urgent</strong></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify; font-family: \'Arial\', sans-serif; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 16px; color: #333;\">Disease, like a cunning hunter lurking in the dark, is always ready to attack us. Its presence is silent but incredibly powerful. Once we ignore it, it can rapidly spread and become a deadly threat to our lives. Supplementing peptides, an effective tool for health management, is one of the important weapons for us to fight against disease and maintain health.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify; font-family: \'Arial\', sans-serif; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 16px; color: #333;\">As the name suggests, supplementing peptides means replenishing the peptides our body needs. The human body naturally contains small molecule peptides, but as we age, these peptides gradually decrease, leading to a decline in bodily functions. Therefore, timely supplementation of peptides is crucial for maintaining good health.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify; font-family: \'Arial\', sans-serif; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 16px; color: #333;\">Small molecule peptides act as attentive guardians, building a solid barrier for our health, improving our resistance to external diseases, helping the body absorb nutrients better, and preventing the occurrence of chronic diseases.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify; font-family: \'Arial\', sans-serif; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 16px; color: #333;\">Remember, health is our precious wealth. Only by maintaining good health can we enjoy life and pursue our dreams. Without health, we cannot enjoy the beauty of life, accompany our families, or realize our dreams.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify; font-family: \'Arial\', sans-serif; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 16px; color: #333;\">Therefore, for yourself, for your family, and for your loved ones, start taking care of your health now! In this era full of challenges and opportunities, let’s join hands and move forward together, using peptides as our health management tool to protect our health.</p>', 2, '/api/personal-heath/v1.0/file/getFile?fileName=news pic/2.jpg', NULL, 1, '2024-09-02 15:18:00', 1);
INSERT INTO `news` VALUES (3, 'Health Care Tips for the Xiao Xue Season', '<p style=\"text-align: justify; font-family: \'Arial\', sans-serif; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 16px; color: #333;\">With the arrival of Xiao Xue, on the 21st, the National Health Commission held a press conference on the theme of \"Seasonal Climate and Health\", addressing issues related to the prevention and control of winter respiratory diseases.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify; font-family: \'Arial\', sans-serif; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 16px; color: #333;\">After the Xiao Xue solar term, the temperature gradually drops, and respiratory infectious diseases enter a peak period. Among children\'s respiratory diseases, Mycoplasma pneumonia is particularly common. Dr. Wang Quan, a pediatrician at Beijing Children\'s Hospital, explained that Mycoplasma pneumonia is most common in children aged 5 and above, although it can also affect children under 5. Symptoms are primarily respiratory, including fever, cough, sore throat, headache, runny nose, nasal congestion, sneezing, and ear pain. Some children, especially infants, may experience wheezing, and some may also have symptoms such as vomiting and diarrhea.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify; font-family: \'Arial\', sans-serif; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 16px; color: #333;\">Experts remind that if a child has persistent high fever, it often indicates a more severe condition, and it is recommended to seek medical attention promptly.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify; font-family: \'Arial\', sans-serif; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 16px; color: #333;\">Many children will continue to cough after being infected with a respiratory disease, with the cough persisting even after the infection has been controlled. Dr. Wang Quan explained that post-infection cough refers to a persistent cough that appears after a respiratory infection and may be caused by viruses, bacteria, or Mycoplasma pneumonia. This cough may be related to damage to the airway mucosa, airway hyperresponsiveness, airway inflammation, or gastroesophageal reflux.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify; font-family: \'Arial\', sans-serif; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 16px; color: #333;\">Experts state that since post-infection cough is self-limiting, most children will see symptoms alleviate within a few weeks. Therefore, if the symptoms are mild, no special treatment is needed. For children with more severe symptoms or persistent cough, treatment should be conducted under a doctor\'s guidance, following prescribed medical advice, avoiding unnecessary medications, and monitoring the child\'s symptoms for any changes, with timely medical consultations as needed.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify; font-family: \'Arial\', sans-serif; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 16px; color: #333;\">As the temperature continues to drop, the risk of flu, Mycoplasma pneumonia, respiratory syncytial virus (RSV) infections, and other respiratory infectious diseases increases. There is a possibility of multiple respiratory diseases occurring simultaneously or co-circulating.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify; font-family: \'Arial\', sans-serif; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 16px; color: #333;\">\"Although the pathogens of these diseases differ, their transmission routes are similar, primarily through respiratory droplets and contact transmission, with infected individuals as the main source of transmission.\" Dr. Chang Zhaorui, a researcher at the Chinese Center for Disease Control and Prevention, said that the public can take various measures to reduce the risk of respiratory infectious diseases and achieve multi-disease prevention. Good personal hygiene habits, maintaining a clean and ventilated living and working environment, wearing masks when necessary, and enhancing physical health through a balanced diet, moderate exercise, and sufficient sleep can help. Reducing contact with people exhibiting respiratory symptoms and conducting health monitoring are also essential.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify; font-family: \'Arial\', sans-serif; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 16px; color: #333;\">Experts suggest that vaccination remains the most cost-effective and efficient way to prevent infectious diseases. For those diseases that can be prevented by vaccines, vaccination should be carried out early according to the vaccination schedule, especially for children, the elderly, and individuals with chronic underlying health conditions.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify; font-family: \'Arial\', sans-serif; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 16px; color: #333;\">\"Currently, China has established a sentinel surveillance system for acute respiratory infectious diseases targeting 15 common respiratory pathogens, such as the flu virus and respiratory syncytial virus,\" said Dr. Chang. This system enables timely monitoring of trends and pathogen spectra of respiratory infectious diseases, effectively supporting clinical treatment and disease prevention, safeguarding public health.</p>', 2, '/api/personal-heath/v1.0/file/getFile?fileName=news pic/3.jpg', NULL, 1, '2024-09-03 14:27:51', 1);
INSERT INTO `news` VALUES (4, 'Sichuan Tianquan County Hospital of Traditional Chinese Medicine Doctor Chen Huaijiong\'s Commitment to Low-Cost Medical Care and Promoting Traditional Chinese Medicine', '<p style=\"text-align: justify; font-family: \'Arial\', sans-serif; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 16px; color: #333;\">Every morning, many people queue outside the Sichuan Tianquan County Hospital of Traditional Chinese Medicine, waiting for their turn to see Doctor Chen Huaijiong.</p>\r\n <p style=\"text-align: justify; font-family: \'Arial\', sans-serif; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 16px; color: #333;\">Born in the 1940s into a family of doctors, Chen Huaijiong officially became the third-generation successor of the Chen family orthopedics practice at the age of 15. Having grown up watching his family heal and treat patients, he took up the mantle of continuing this medical tradition. The Chen family orthopedics was well-known locally, with patients traveling from afar, sometimes hundreds of miles, to seek treatment. Chen Huaijiong has always insisted on offering low-cost or even free consultations for those who visit his practice, and has frequently volunteered to conduct medical outreach in rural areas or participate in free clinics.</p>\r\n <p style=\"text-align: justify; font-family: \'Arial\', sans-serif; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 16px; color: #333;\">In 1975, the Tianquan County People\'s Government established a traditional Chinese medicine surgery hospital (which later merged with the Tianquan County Traditional Chinese Medicine Hospital). To better serve the public, Chen Huaijiong donated the diagnostic methods, prescriptions, and clinic of the Chen family orthopedics to the hospital. Chen remarked, \"Medical resources are meant to serve the people, and saving lives is the most important thing. Promoting traditional Chinese medicine should not rely on one person or family; it requires open inheritance and innovative development to truly realize its potential.\" From that point onward, Chen Huaijiong became a doctor at a public hospital.</p>\r\n <p style=\"text-align: justify; font-family: \'Arial\', sans-serif; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 16px; color: #333;\">Chen Huaijiong\'s compassion and dedication to serving his patients helped establish the tradition of low-cost care at Tianquan County Traditional Chinese Medicine Hospital. Initially, his consultation fee for expert appointments was the same as regular appointments—just 0.5 yuan. It wasn\'t until 2005, when the hospital\'s registration and billing system was upgraded, that the fee increased to 1 yuan, and it has remained unchanged since then. \"I want the people here to be able to afford their medical care and receive good treatment,\" said Chen. One summer, an elderly patient from Neijiang, Sichuan, came for treatment. After learning about the patient\'s financial situation, Chen decided to waive all treatment costs. After the patient recovered, Chen personally paid for their transportation back home.</p>\r\n <p style=\"text-align: justify; font-family: \'Arial\', sans-serif; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 16px; color: #333;\">At the hospital\'s outpatient clinic, a doctor treated a patient with shoulder and cervical syndrome using cupping therapy, massage, and applying a special herbal patch, charging only 8 yuan. Another patient received orthopedic realignment and splinting, for a charge of 125 yuan. Chen Ruolei, the hospital director and fourth-generation successor of the Chen family orthopedics, explained: \"At our hospital, while ensuring treatment effectiveness, we aim to reduce costs. If traditional Chinese medicine methods like observation, questioning, listening, and palpation can resolve the issue, we avoid using equipment or performing surgeries.\"</p>\r\n <p style=\"text-align: justify; font-family: \'Arial\', sans-serif; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 16px; color: #333;\">\"Tianquan County Traditional Chinese Medicine Hospital has been actively exploring ways to maximize the unique advantages of traditional Chinese medicine to ensure patients recover effectively and spend less,\" said Tian Xingjun, Party Secretary and Director of the Sichuan Provincial Administration of Traditional Chinese Medicine.</p>\r\n <p style=\"text-align: justify; font-family: \'Arial\', sans-serif; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 16px; color: #333;\">In 2023, Tianquan County Traditional Chinese Medicine Hospital\'s outpatient department treated 623,500 patients, with a sharp increase in visitors from outside the province. Wang Qiutao, Director of the Tianquan County Health Bureau, stated that local government support for the hospital has increased in recent years, with investments totaling 300 million yuan to establish a comprehensive center covering 80 acres and 80,000 square meters of business space.</p>\r\n <p style=\"text-align: justify; font-family: \'Arial\', sans-serif; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 16px; color: #333;\">Every morning, nearly 80-year-old Chen Huaijiong arrives on time at the hospital, working nearly every day of the year. Diagnosis, prescriptions, applying medication... this esteemed doctor, named one of the top ten renowned traditional Chinese doctors in Sichuan, continues to work diligently on the frontlines of healthcare. The corridor outside the orthopedic treatment room is packed with patients traveling from afar to seek his expertise.</p>\r\n <p style=\"text-align: justify; font-family: \'Arial\', sans-serif; line-height: 1.8; font-size: 16px; color: #333;\">For Chen Huaijiong, his commitment to medicine and his compassion for patients has never wavered.</p>', 1, '/api/personal-heath/v1.0/file/getFile?fileName=news pic/4.jpg', NULL, 1, '2024-07-14 14:29:09', 1);
INSERT INTO `news` VALUES (5, '10 Health \"Gold Standards\"', '<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Whether a person is healthy</p>\r\n <p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Various common body index values are the most direct way to judge health</p>\r\n <p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The normal values of the following body indicators</p>\r\n <p style=\"text-align: justify;\">And healthy lifestyles to maintain normal values</p>\r\n <p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Everyone should know this!</p>\r\n <p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Quickly check it against yourself!</p>\r\n <p style=\"text-align: justify;\">10 Health \"Gold Standards\"</p>\r\n <p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Blood Pressure Standards</p>\r\n <p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Systolic pressure &lt; 120 mmHg, Diastolic pressure &lt; 80 mmHg</p>\r\n <p style=\"text-align: justify;\">According to the \"Chinese Hypertension Prevention and Treatment Guidelines (2018 Revision)\" issued by the Cardiovascular Disease Branch of the Chinese Medical Association and other organizations, the normal range for blood pressure in adults in China is: Systolic pressure &lt; 120 mmHg, Diastolic pressure &lt; 80 mmHg.</p>\r\n <p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Abnormal blood pressure not only affects vascular health but also impacts the heart and brain. The \"Chinese Hypertension Patient Education Guidelines\" points out that high blood pressure is the most important risk factor for stroke, and 70% of stroke patients in China have hypertension.</p>\r\n <p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><img src=\"https://p3-sign.toutiaoimg.com/pgc-image/SUnEYkXADWQXzc~noop.image?_iz=58558&from=article.pc_detail&lk3s=953192f4&x-expires=1721543649&x-signature=RuB5B1ApqxK6xu2fLl%2Bvs%2Bt4m%2BM%3D\" alt=\"\" data-href=\"\" style=\"height: auto;\"></p>\r\n <p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Image Source: \"Chinese Hypertension Prevention and Treatment Guidelines (2018 Revision)\"</p>', 3, '/api/personal-heath/v1.0/file/getFile?fileName=news pic/5.jpg', NULL, 0, '2024-09-05 14:34:58', 1);
INSERT INTO `news` VALUES (7, 'The Fast-Paced Modern Life, Like an Invisible Hand', '<p> </p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">In the past, with the rapid development of China\'s economy, many people\'s living standards and material conditions have greatly improved. However, behind this rapid growth lie some overlooked issues, with health being one of the most prominent. As economic growth slows and society gradually becomes more harmonious, people are beginning to realize that health is a more important part of life.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>The Health Data of Chinese People is Shocking!</strong></p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Through careful collection and sorting, we have obtained a detailed set of data regarding the health status of Chinese people. These are not just cold statistics, but rather vivid lives telling us the preciousness of health.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Hypertension – 160 to 170 million people</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Hyperlipidemia – over 100 million people</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Diabetic patients – 92.4 million people</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Overweight or obese – 70 million to 200 million people</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Abnormal blood lipids – 160 million people</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Fatty liver disease patients – 120 million people</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">On average, every 30 seconds, one person is diagnosed with cancer,</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">On average, every 30 seconds, one person is diagnosed with diabetes,</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">On average, every 30 seconds, at least one person dies from cardiovascular and cerebrovascular diseases.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Behind these cold numbers lie the pain and helplessness of countless families. They silently tell a cruel truth: in the busy pursuit of money and material pleasures, we often neglect our health. When health issues silently approach like an undercurrent, we are only awakened when it is too late!</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Establishing a Good Health Concept</strong></p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The fast-paced modern life is like an invisible hand pushing us forward, but at the same time, it is subtly changing our lifestyle and eating habits. Irregular schedules, high-fat, high-salt diets, etc., are silently eroding our health, causing the shadow of chronic diseases to gradually overshadow our lives.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">What is even more severe is that our awareness of health remains insufficient. In the past, people focused solely on economic development and the improvement of material conditions, forgetting that health is the foundation of life. What we need is not only the continuous advancement of medical technology but also a deeper understanding of health concepts and the conscious cultivation of healthy behaviors.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Health is urgent for everyone. We must cherish our bodies and always remind ourselves that health is the most important. Don’t wait until health is lost to regret!</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Supplementing Peptides is Urgent</strong></p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Diseases are like a sly hunter lurking in the shadows, ready to attack us at any time. It exists silently but is extremely powerful. Once we neglect it, it can quickly spread, becoming a raging fire that threatens our lives. Supplementing peptides, this health management tool, is an important weapon in our fight against disease and for maintaining health.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Peptide supplementation, as the name suggests, is about replenishing the peptides needed by the body. The human body already contains small peptides, but as we age, the amount of peptides decreases, leading to the gradual decline of various bodily functions. Therefore, timely supplementation of peptides is of great importance for maintaining health.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Small peptides act like a thoughtful guardian, building a solid barrier to protect our health and enhancing our resistance against external diseases. They also help the body absorb nutrients better and prevent chronic diseases from occurring.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">Remember, health is our precious wealth. Only by having a healthy body can we enjoy life and pursue our dreams. Without health, we cannot enjoy the beauty of life, be with our families, or realize our dreams.</p><p style=\"text-align: justify;\">So, for ourselves, for our families, and for our loved ones, let’s start health maintenance now! In this era full of challenges and opportunities, let us move forward hand in hand, using peptide supplementation as a health management tool to protect our path to health.</p>', 3, '/api/personal-heath/v1.0/file/getFile?fileName=news pic/7.jpg', NULL, NULL, '2024-09-07 16:10:35', 1);
